With **.NET 10 SDK**, you get native MTP support in `dotnet test` — no `TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport` needed. That property is only for .NET 9 and earlier.

**Setup:** Add a `test` section to your `global.json`:

```json
{
  "sdk": {
    "version": "10.0.100"
  },
  "test": {
    "runner": "Microsoft.Testing.Platform"
  }
}
```

That's it. In this mode, MTP arguments are passed directly (no `--` separator needed):

```shell
dotnet test --report-trx --filter "Category=Unit"
```

You still need the framework-specific runner enablement (`EnableMSTestRunner`, `EnableNUnitRunner`, etc.) and `<OutputType>Exe</OutputType>` in your test projects — the `global.json` setting just tells `dotnet test` to speak MTP protocol instead of VSTest.

